Problem Statement:
Community mobilization
Fragmented environmental community efforts
Sustainable & updated education initiatives on climate 
change
Verification of impact transparently
Rewards for continued participation
Climate change profoundly impacts daily life across Kenya. 
The North faces collapsing water tables and severe drought, 
while farmers endure devastating crop losses from erratic 
rainfall. Urban areas grapple with escalating floods and 
mounting waste crises.
Despite widespread tree-planting initiatives, their long-term 
success is often uncertain. As the Green Belt Movement, with 
over 51 million trees planted, emphasizes: "Trees only thrive 
if communities remain deeply engaged long after 
planting."
What's Holding Us Back?
Fragmented Mobilization
Lack of a cohesive system to unite 
diverse community groups
Disconnected Efforts
Environmental projects operate in 
isolation, hindering collective impact
Limited Education & 
Awareness Initiatives
Absence of continuous learning and 
capacity-building opportunities
Opaque Verification
Insufficient mechanisms for 
transparent and credible climate 
impact tracking
Reward & Recognition 
Incentives
No structured reward or recognition 
systems to sustain community 
participation
Outdated Policies
Policy change to support the new 
initiatives such as vision 2030 
Environmental initiatives, COP30 
global initiatives
OUR SOLUTION
Gang Green is a unified, gamified platform that mobilizes 
Kenya9s communities, verifies environmental impact, and 
rewards sustained climate action.
Driving Transformative Change Through 
Innovation
Track 相 Alignment: Cultivating Public Awareness & 
Sustained Engagement
Dynamic Community Hub
Our interactive platform transforms 
climate action into social capital, 
fostering peer-to-peer inspiration and 
tangible accountability within 
communities.
Engaging Gamified Learning
Participants earn valuable Green Coins 
by completing compelling climate 
missions and educational modules, 
thoughtfully designed for all ages and 
literacy levels.
Empowering Digital 
Marketplace
Communities gain direct access to 
essential eco-products, vital native 
seedlings, practical composting kits, and 
expert environmental training resources.
Strategic Civic Engagement
Our public petition tools empower communities to directly 
influence and shape critical environmental policy decisions 
at both county and national levels.
Localized Verification-as-a-Service (VaaS)
Leveraging global best practices, our VaaS is powerfully 
localized through partnerships with Kenya's most trusted 
on-ground organizations: GBM, WMF, and KFS.
Business Model: Sustainable Growth, Tangible 
Impact
Our innovative hybrid revenue model integrates B2C, B2B, and B2G streams, meticulously designed for scalable growth and 
enduring environmental impact.
Verification-as-a-Service
Provide precise, third-party 
verification for corporate CSR 
planting, comprehensive ESG 
reporting, and robust county-level 
climate monitoring systems.
Sponsored Campaigns
Empower brands to sponsor 
high-impact climate challenges, 
like the '1 Million Trees 
Challenge,' engaging directly 
with a dedicated, 
environmentally conscious 
audience.
Marketplace 
Commissions
Drive revenue through commissions 
on curated eco-friendly products, 
verified seedling sales from trusted 
merchants, and specialized 
environmental education programs.
Green Coins Economy
Cultivate a dynamic 'Green Coins' rewards system, 
incentivizing user participation while offering partners 
premium marketplace visibility and strategic sponsorship 
opportunities.
Advanced Data & Analytics
Deliver sophisticated analytics dashboards and impact 
reports for counties, NGOs, and corporations, enabling 
data-driven environmental tracking and strategic 
decision-making.
Proven Success Models: Gang Green builds on the foundations of successful platforms like Tree-Nation, Wren, and 
Litterati. We adapt these proven sustainable revenue models to Kenya's unique climate ecosystem, ensuring both mission 
integrity and long-term viability.
